{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "h6-eval-no-notes",
  "title": "Offline Evaluation Harness",
  "description": "Offline evaluation harness orchestration, read left to right, top row then bottom row.\n\n- **Pinned Suite** (green): frozen scenario versions (a wording change creates v2 instead of editing v1) and the run fingerprint (revision, config, prompt and rubric versions). The fingerprint stamps the scorecard.\n- **Bounded Execution** (violet): scheduler fans out to a bounded worker pool that runs steps in order against an isolated SUT (never prod). The scenario outcome decision separates infra faults (orange: retry, re-run through the scheduler) from SUT-behavior failures (red: recorded, then the worker continues). Completed scenarios yield transcript + final artifact.\n- **Grading** (teal): the Graders subsection holds the criterion graders (request + transcript), the artifact-only grader (artifact only) and the global concurrency limit that caps them. Every verdict passes the evidence check; a verdict without evidence is retried once and the re-graded verdict is checked again, and it is flagged if the retry fails. Checked verdicts are retained with their evidence.\n- **Scorecard & Baseline Comparison** (pink): assembler merges valid verdicts; the scorecard is compared to the baseline only on a fingerprint match; movements crossing the threshold are narrated.\n- **Retained Evidence** (orange): run results keep infra faults and product regressions apart; artifacts, transcripts and verdicts are kept for dispute review.\n- **Baseline** (yellow): promoting a run makes it the baseline that supplies the next comparison.\n\nNode colors: teal = harness actors, violet = graders, blue = records, yellow = gates, orange = infra faults/retries, red = product failures and invalid outcomes, green = promotion.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
